From c69243a283ad90903ab9f5daac179619884c206f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CustomKIMI <customkimi@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:36:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] customkimi: show the gemini forwarder's usage in /usage
 and the web UI

The gemini forwarder's GET /usage has the muse forwarder's shape, so the
muse usage feature now covers both: /usage adds one panel per configured
forwarder (" Muse ", " Gemini "), and the web pill is named after the
forwarder serving the open session's model. A forwarder is a provider
whose key variable is MUSE_FORWARDER_KEY or GEMINI_FORWARDER_KEY; the
gemini forwarder is usually configured with the muse key, so which one
answered is read from the reply (identity.agy_version). Gemini reports
two quota groups (Gemini models; Claude and GPT models): the panel shows
the weekly and 5h bars of each, and the pill shows those of the model's
own group. Reset times may be ISO strings as well as UNIX seconds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
